# Wave W17-AD (Amber Sea — North): shrine rock — a deep-shadow boulder standing in the shipped sea, dark in the channel, carrying a sparse lantern-warm glint at its top register — Sanctum’s lantern light reaching the lane’s last stones, drawn in the kind at art layer only (design: lantern light on the water at the far end). North’s own rock — split from East’s pale worked stone by light entire and from the shrine isles’ own rocks by office: this stone stands IN the lane as its last marker; the isles themselves are out of program and unbuilt by this wave.
